---
title: Mnemonics
layout: base.njk
permalink: /tools/mnemonics/
summary: Memory aids for the things that must be recalled cold — ordering, flag sets, and the distinctions that fail under time pressure.
---
<h1>Mnemonics</h1>
<p class="muted">These cover the material where <em>ordering</em> or an exact set is the thing that fails under pressure —
not comprehension. Each one is collapsed by default: try to produce the sequence before you open it.</p>

{% for d in domains %}
{% set mine = drills.mnemonics | byDomain(d.id) %}
{% if mine.length %}
<h2>{{ d.short or d.title }} <span class="pill">{{ d.weight }}%</span></h2>
{% for m in mine %}
<div class="card">
  <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px">{{ m.title }}</h3>
  <p style="margin:0 0 10px"><strong>{{ m.mnemonic }}</strong></p>
  <details>
    <summary>Show the sequence</summary>
    <table>
      <tbody>
      {% for step in m.sequence %}
        <tr><th style="white-space:nowrap">{{ step.key }}</th><td><code>{{ step.text }}</code></td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="small muted"><strong>Why:</strong> {{ m.why }}</p>
  </details>
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

<p class="small muted">Rendered from <code>data/mnemonics.json</code>, which is also what the PDF build reads — one source,
two outputs.</p>
